 ## Background
-HyperINR was introduced by Qi Wu, David Bauer, Yuyang Chen, and Kwan-Liu Ma from the University of California, Davis. It was published on arXiv on 9 Apr 2023 (arXiv:2304.04188v1) [S1, unofficial]. The method addresses the limitation of standard INRs, which require millions of operations per forward pass, hindering interactive visualization [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [InstantNGP Network Architecture](5049-instantngp-network-architecture.md) by using multiresolution hash encoding [S1, unofficial]. It is used for Novel View Synthesis (NVS), Temporal Super-Resolution of Volume Data (TSR), and Volume Rendering with Dynamic Global Shadows (DGS) [S1, unofficial].
+HyperINR was introduced by Qi Wu, David Bauer, Yuyang Chen, and Kwan-Liu Ma from the University of California, Davis [S1, unofficial]. It was published on arXiv on 9 Apr 2023 (arXiv:2304.04188v1) [S1, unofficial]. The method addresses the limitation of standard INRs, which require millions of operations per forward pass, hindering interactive visualization [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [InstantNGP Network Architecture](5049-instantngp-network-architecture.md) by using multiresolution hash encoding [S1, unofficial]. It is used for Novel View Synthesis (NVS), Temporal Super-Resolution of Volume Data (TSR), and Volume Rendering with Dynamic Global Shadows (DGS) [S1, unofficial].
 
